      "claim": "The earliest stone tools (Oldowan) date to approximately 2.6 million years ago, predating the emergence of anatomically modern humans (AMH) by over 2 million years.",
      "evidence": "Archaeological sites like Gona (Ethiopia) and Lomekwi 3 (Kenya) provide evidence of stone tool use dating back to 2.6-3.3 million years ago, whereas AMH fossils (e.g., Jebel Irhoud) date to ~300,000 years ago.",
