      "claim": "The 'improvement' in stone tool technology is a continuous process spanning millions of years (Oldowan -> Acheulean -> Levallois/Middle Paleolithic), meaning the characteristic of having 'improved' technologies existed long before the Upper Paleolithic.",
      "evidence": "Acheulean handaxes appear ~1.7 million years ago; Levallois techniques appear ~300,000+ years ago. These are distinct technological improvements over earlier modes and predate the Upper Paleolithic (~50,000 years ago).",
