      "claim": "Elaborate burials, large permanent settlements, and widespread symbolic art are primarily associated with the Upper Paleolithic or later periods, not the deep past.",
      "evidence": "Cave art (e.g., Chauvet) is ~30-40kya; elaborate burials are rare before the Middle/Upper Paleolithic; dense permanent villages are a Neolithic phenomenon (~10kya). While isolated early symbolic items exist (e.g., Blombos beads ~75kya), they do not constitute the widespread 'production of art' characteristic of the Upper Paleolithic, nor do they predate AMH as a general category.",
